.TH scan_fromhex 3
.SH NAME
scan_fromhex \- convert a single hexadecimal character to its integer value
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/scan.h>

int \fBscan_fromhex\fR(int \fIc\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan_fromhex\fR converts a single character \fIc\fR, representing a
hexadecimal digit, into its corresponding integer value (0-15).
It handles '0'-'9', 'a'-'f', and 'A'-'F'.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the integer value of the hexadecimal digit, or -1 if the character
is not a valid hexadecimal digit.